  {
    "sha": "9c72cb9b5b589f05151a4c0ad547cb1e71c38a81",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOJbajnNoAKDljNzJjYjliNWI1ODlmMDUxNTFhNGMwYWQ1NDdjYjFlNzFjMzhhODE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Cesar Rodas",
        "email": "cesar@rodasm.com.py",
        "date": "2026-04-09T22:14:58Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "thesimplekid",
        "email": "tsk@thesimplekid.com",
        "date": "2026-05-12T02:15:36Z"
      },
      "message": "Consolidate FFI runtime handling into RuntimeGuard\n\nThe ad-hoc Handle::try_current() / Runtime::new() pattern was duplicated across\nevery FFI constructor (sqlite, postgres, wallet_repository).  Extract a shared\nRuntimeGuard that detects an existing Tokio runtime or creates one, and keeps\nit alive for the lifetime of the FFI object so that async pool operations\n(semaphore acquire) work in foreign-language contexts that lack a Tokio\nreactor.\n\nAlso replace tokio::time::timeout in the connection pool with a\ntry_acquire_owned fast-path + plain acquire_owned await, since the timeout\nrequired the Tokio time driver which UniFFI's Python bridge does not provide.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "15dea6fc8583f55915398277d1d7bafaf77b98e0",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cashubtc/cdk/git/trees/15dea6fc8583f55915398277d1d7bafaf77b98e0"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cashubtc/cdk/git/commits/9c72cb9b5b589f05151a4c0ad547cb1e71c38a81",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQT7FBefWxISmS43iYljrW0Ju/53gwUCagKNSAAKCRBjrW0Ju/53\ng4lzAP9Rxskm3F40EhOFZgRC9M0hZknVbqItfT06mm3aEMpBZQD/R63F8A+uA3Aw\nUh0ZQKnkOTJPeJ1a4Vk9c2C3/dqHtQk=\n=7Mgf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----",
        "payload": "tree 15dea6fc8583f55915398277d1d7bafaf77b98e0\nparent 128e68d42c94c54a5b6bdcef182258f14cfe5dba\nauthor Cesar Rodas <cesar@rodasm.com.py> 1775772898 -0300\ncommitter thesimplekid <tsk@thesimplekid.com> 1778552136 -0400\nchange-id zlysulwlmuzmouszooxmvtlmmnzkylrv\n\nConsolidate FFI runtime handling into RuntimeGuard\n\nThe ad-hoc Handle::try_current() / Runtime::new() pattern was duplicated across\nevery FFI constructor (sqlite, postgres, wallet_repository).  Extract a shared\nRuntimeGuard that detects an existing Tokio runtime or creates one, and keeps\nit alive for the lifetime of the FFI object so that async pool operations\n(semaphore acquire) work in foreign-language contexts that lack a Tokio\nreactor.\n\nAlso replace tokio::time::timeout in the connection pool with a\ntry_acquire_owned fast-path + plain acquire_owned await, since the timeout\nrequired the Tokio time driver which UniFFI's Python bridge does not provide.\n",
        "verified_at": "2026-05-12T02:15:47Z"
      }
    },
